  "description": "\nDemolition of existing ground floor conservatory, cantilevered balcony and outrigger and removal of lower ground storage and boiler/plant spaces.\n\nConstruction of two storey extension, comprising dining room at ground level and utility with snug at lower ground. An external balcony is proposed to the rear. \nThe proposed rear extension is to extend to the building line and outside corner of the existing outrigger, infilling the space between the outrigger and Party Wall of the adjoining property. The eaves height  is to match that of the adjoining property at No 84.\n\nA new internal staircase will connect the two levels.\n\nAt lower ground the existing levels allow for a floor to ceiling height of 2 metres. \n\nThe side access is to remain as existing whilst the external brick stairs would be modified to accommodate the balcony.\n\nThe balcony is to be a freestanding metal structure extending 2 metres from the rear of the building and set approximately 900mm from the boundary with 84. A timber clad privacy screen is proposed between the balcony and neighbouring property of No 84\n\nThe exterior is to be brick built, with brickwork and bond to match existing, windows to be powdercoated aluminum. Rainwater goods black upvc to match existing. \n\nAn opening roof light is proposed to the new extension flat roof, to provide natural cross ventilation to the new room beneath.\n",
